# Specs and implementation plans. Kept on disk because they are how this project
# gets worked on, but untracked: they are agent working documents, not
# documentation. They referenced an Obsidian vault and a DESIGN-STANDARDS.md
# that no reader of this repo can open, and at 296KB they outweighed the entire
# source tree on the repo landing page.
docs/superpowers/

# Agent context. Kept on disk because it is how this project gets worked on, but
# untracked for the same reason as the plans above: it references an Obsidian
# vault and a DESIGN-STANDARDS.md that no reader of this repo can open, and it
# carries a lot of internal "this was wrong twice" narrative that is valuable to
# a maintainer and noise to everyone else.
CLAUDE.md

# The cask lives in Stixum/homebrew-tap. A second copy here would drift out of
# sync with the one that actually gets installed.
docs/homebrew/

# Sparkle EdDSA private key, if ever exported. The key lives in the login
# keychain; an export on disk must never reach the repo.
*private-key*
*.p8
